SPEC = {'file': 'cover_capgemini_accelerate_data_analytics', 'label': 'Capgemini Accelerate Graduate Programme, Enterprise Data and Analytics', 'center': True, 'paras': ['I am writing to apply for the Accelerate Graduate Programme in Enterprise Data \\& Analytics at Capgemini. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This programme is close to what I have actually done: working with data and AI on client problems, and turning the results into decisions people act on.', 'What attracts me most to Capgemini is the chance to work on data and AI problems across many clients and industries while being trained in a structured programme. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.', 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked.', 'Before TikTok I worked as a Data Scientist Intern at DS Digital Technology on a medical AI engagement, where I built Python pipelines that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and multi-step workflows and automated the processing and scoring of over 2,400 records. I designed the evaluation framework around it, a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and I co-built a scientifically reviewed knowledge graph and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved output quality.', 'On client work, at Ipsos Strategy3 I turned more than 80 expert interviews into quantitative insight and built market-sizing models with the research and strategy teams. My dissertation builds predictive and causal models on 458,840 UK Biobank participants and is delivered as a deployed Streamlit application so that people can run scenarios without touching the code. Explaining results clearly to people who do not want the method is something I have done at Ipsos Strategy3 and with pharmaceutical client stakeholders.', "Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I could contribute to Capgemini's Enterprise Data \\& Analytics team. I am based in London. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship."]}
